", "Incumbent Eugene Vindman (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Representative Eugene Vindman enters the general election as a clear favorite in a district that leans Democratic by about two points. He has raised roughly $16.3 million and holds more than $5 million on hand, while Republican Doug Ollivant has raised about $389,000. No independent public polls are available, but ten editorial ratings place the race between Likely and Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price a Democratic win near 96 percent.\n\nThe campaign has centered on affordability, and Vindman faces five challengers, including independents and a Libertarian who may siphon votes. A strong Republican national environment could narrow the margin, but the incumbent's financial and institutional advantages remain substantial. The expected outcome is a double-digit Democratic win, with somewhat wider uncertainty because direct polling in the district is absent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 13.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9562, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9406, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9612, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9637, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9667, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9827, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9746, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9681, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9696, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9686, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9744, "margin": 13.5}, {"date"